<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kathiawar Agency</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as British Kathiawar Agency</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a> Agency was the British political agency, based at Rajkot, that supervised the more than two hundred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> and chiefships of the Kathiawar peninsula in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, from great states such as Junagadh and Bhavnagar to tiny talukas. It settled disputes and tribute owed to Baroda and the British. In 1924 it was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-india-states-agency">Western India States Agency</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kathiawar-agency.jpg" alt="Kathiawar Agency" width="320" height="288" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John George Bartholomew · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baroda_state_1909.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
